{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_15-41-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor c in d['question_candidates']:\n    if c['id']=='1dc85f2220ab4a6b9ff4e16a1ac749a2':\n        print(json.dumps(c['question'], indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"audit_spec_version\": 5,\n \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n \"question\": \"Can a node that adopted a configuration whose log entry was never durably stored later commit that configuration as its committed configuration, for example after regaining leadership with the vote of a fresh peer?\",\n \"importance\": \"A committed configuration that no log entry supports would make this node and its peers disagree about the voter set that defines quorum, election eligibility and the leader lease; a node could then treat a server as a voter (or a previous voter as removed) without any agreed log entry, which is a consensus-safety consequence of the confirmed configuration-durability defect rather than only a local inconsistency.\",\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"SR-APPEND-CONFIG\",\n  \"SR-NEXT-CONFIG\",\n  \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\",\n  \"SR-COMMITMENT\"\n ],\n \"participants\": [],\n \"objects\": [],\n \"contexts\": [\n  \"a node whose configuration entry write failed and which therefore holds a latest configuration not present in its log\",\n  \"a fresh peer that joins with an empty configuration and log\"\n ],\n \"event_paths\": [\n  \"AddVoter fails its StoreLogs, dispatchLogs answers the error and sets state Follower, and appendConfigurationEntry still publishes the new latest configuration\",\n  \"the follower heartbeat timer observes latestIndex different from committedIndex and the local server being a voter of the latest configuration, then transitions to Candidate\",\n  \"electSelf requests votes for the next term from the latest configuration's voters and the fresh peer grants one\",\n  \"the leader commits an entry of its term and the commit path marks configurations.latest as committed because latestIndex is now within the commit index\"\n ],\n \"activity_classes\": [\n  \"A2\",\n  \"A4\"\n ],\n \"behavior_ids\": [\n  \"b-candidate-election\"\n ],\n \"fact_ids\": [\n  \"f-config-membership\"\n ],\n \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n  \"b-config-change\": \"establishes the latest configuration from the leader-side change path whose durable write failed\",\n  \"b-commit-quorum\": \"consumes the voter set of the latest configuration when deciding what can be committed\"\n },\n \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"the node alone cannot command a majority of the phantom voter set, so adopting the configuration does not by itself commit it\",\n  \"processConfigurationLogEntry is the only intended writer of configuration state from an actual log entry\"\n ],\n \"unknowns\": [\n  \"Whether a fresh peer with an empty configuration actually grants the vote to the node holding the phantom configuration\",\n  \"Whether the node can satisfy the commitment gate for an entry of its own term in that configuration and thereby mark the phantom configuration committed\"\n ],\n \"priority\": 3,\n \"trigger_rationale\": \"The confirmed check stopped at the post-failure state. The next discriminating step is whether the adopted configuration can reach the committed state: the follower heartbeat path admits a campaign whenever latestIndex differs from committedIndex and the local server is a voter of the latest configuration, so a node in that state may campaign under the phantom voter set; a fresh peer with an empty configuration has no membership veto and no log to compare against, so whether it grants the vote, and whether the leader can then satisfy the commitment gate for its own term, decides the proposition.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
